  "description": "Convert HTML to PDF in C# using this Docotic.Pdf add-on. Your C# HTML to PDF conversion will produce the pixel-perfect PDF because the add-on uses Chromium during rendering. You get the same web standards compliance as in Google Chrome (R).\n\nUse the add-on to convert HTML to PDF in the C# code of your .NET Core, ASP.NET, Windows Forms, WPF, Xamarin, or Blazor application. The add-on supports .NET 10 - .NET 5, .NET Core 2.0+ and .NET Framework 4.6.1+. You can use the add-on on Windows, Linux, and macOS. It works in Azure and AWS cloud environments and can be used from a Docker container.\n\nThis HTML to PDF converter provides an async API for C# and VB.NET. You can convert HTML strings and files, SVG images, and HTML with CSS and scripts. You can also specify header and footer templates. \n\nThe add-on includes advanced capabilities such as converting password-protected URLs, ignoring SSL errors, and delaying the start of conversion.\n\nFind an overview of the HTML to PDF capabilities of this C# library at https://bitmiracle.com/pdf-library/html-pdf/\n\nTo explore Docotic.Pdf features beyond HTML‑to‑PDF conversion, visit https://bitmiracle.com/pdf-library/help\n\nCore library NuGet package: https://www.nuget.org/packages/BitMiracle.Docotic.Pdf/\n\nThis is a prerelease version with the newest features and latest bug fixes. We have tested it for regressions, and is safe to use in a production environment.",
